E. What NOTWIN would do to the bytes the body actually builds
========================================================================
  site                   byte                               ruling                 -> with NOTWIN
  loop.py:217 _rule      BUILT                              SHIP                   -> RESHAPE
  loop.py:217 _rule      BUILT+CAPPED                       RAISE_BUDGET           -> RESHAPE
  loop.py:217 _rule      BUILT+AMB                          ADD_STATE              -> ADD_STATE
  loop.py:217 _rule      BUILT+AMB+CAPPED                   ADD_STATE              -> ADD_STATE
  loop.py:391 HIDDEN     HIDDEN                             CHANGE_GRANULARITY     -> AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR
  guard.py:491 UNREAD    UNREAD                             ADD_MATERIAL           -> ADD_MATERIAL
  guard.py:612/618       REFUTED                            HARVEST_COUNTEREXAMPLE -> AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR
  guard.py:539           (empty)                            SHIP                   -> RESHAPE
  guard.py:539           CAPPED                             RAISE_BUDGET           -> AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR
  guard.py:539           CAPPED+REFUTED                     RAISE_BUDGET           -> AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR
  distinct body-constructible bytes here: 10
  bytes whose ruling CHANGES when NOTWIN is added: 7/10

========================================================================
F. The one that matters: the shipping byte
========================================================================
  BUILT            -> SHIP
  BUILT+NOTWIN     -> RESHAPE
  BUILT+AMB        -> ADD_STATE
  BUILT+AMB+NOTWIN -> ADD_STATE   (AMB outranks NOTWIN: NOTWIN is INVISIBLE once AMB holds)
  BUILT+CAPPED        -> RAISE_BUDGET
  BUILT+NOTWIN+CAPPED -> RESHAPE
